 This is the help message for the Who's Online global
 command.

WHOHLP {<ESC>[0m
<ESC>[1;36mThis global command tells you who is currently on-line and where they are,
along with other useful information. It is more detailed than /#, and is
used as follows:
<ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG>
<ESC>[36mYou can choose whether or not to have your age displayed to others. Your
current setting <TV:GLO_WILL> display your age.
To allow your age to be displayed, type:
<ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG> ON
<ESC>[36mTo prevent your age from being displayed, type:
<ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG> OFF
<ESC>[36mNormally when you type <ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG><ESC>[36m, your default Who's Online choice will be displayed.
However, you can view a different setting by typing:
<ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG> <#>      where <#> is from <ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_MIN> <ESC>[33mto <ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_MAX>
<ESC>[36mYour current default Who's Online choice is <ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_WHODISP><ESC>[36m.
To change your default Who's Online choice, type:
<ESC>[33m<TV:GLO_WHOSTG> SET <#>  where <#> is from <ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_MIN> <ESC>[33mto <ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_MAX>
} T Who's online help

 This message informs the user of his new setting for
 displaying his age in the Who's Online display.

SHOWAGE {<ESC>[0m
<ESC>[1;36mOk, your setting to display your age to others in Who's Online has been turned
<ESC>[37m<TV:GLO_SHOWAGE><ESC>[36m.
} T Show age setting message

 This message informs the user of his new default Who's
